## 4. Genesis `prev_hash` is undefined for base64 hashes

The old "64 zeros" convention was for hex-encoded hashes. `06-api-contract.md` uses base64. Define in `shared/`:
```
GENESIS_PREV_HASH = base64 encoding of 32 zero bytes
# i.e. base64.b64encode(b"\x00" * 32) == "AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA="
```
The first entry from any agent (`seq = 0`) uses this constant as its `prev_hash`. Document this constant in `shared/` and reference it from `06-api-contract.md`'s entry section.

