## 6. Rejected entries must not cascade-fail everything after them

Currently nothing says what the chain's "good tip" is after a rejection, so every later entry also fails against a broken reference, and one attack floods the whole alert list.

**Decision:** the witness tracks `last_good_seq` / `last_good_hash` separately from "last entry received." Only *accepted* entries advance `last_good_*`. New incoming entries are validated against `last_good_*`, never against a rejected entry. A rejected entry is stored (for audit evidence) and raises exactly one alert; it does not change what the next entry is checked against. Since the agent's own local state is untouched by an attack on the witness's stored data (A1/A2/A10 all tamper with the witness's copy, not the agent), the agent's next real entry continues incrementing normally from its own last successfully-delivered entry and will validate cleanly against `last_good_*`.

Update `06-api-contract.md`'s `/entries` section with this rule, and update item 1's Step 4 rewrite in `02-flow.md` to say the same thing (validate against `last_good_*`, not against the previous arrival regardless of its outcome).

