## 7. No key rotation route — add one

Step 10 rotates keys but `06-api-contract.md` has no endpoint. Add:

### `POST /keys/rotate`
```json
// request
{ "platform_id": "victim-bank-1", "new_public_key": "base64...", "signature": "base64..." }
// signed payload = canonical encoding of {platform_id, new_public_key}, signed with the OLD private key
// response
{ "status": "rotated", "key_id": "agent-key-1", "effective_from_seq": 101 }
```
Witness verifies the signature against the *currently registered* key for that `platform_id` before accepting — this is what makes the rotation itself provable (old key attests to the new one) and prevents a random third party from rotating someone else's keys. After rotation, the old `key_id` stays valid for verifying *past* entries signed before `effective_from_seq`; only new entries must use the new `key_id`.

