## 11. T2d needs a real comparison tool, not just `/verify` alone

`GET /verify` only re-checks the witness's *own* stored copy against itself — it has nothing to compare against the agent's local copy, so T2d (local vs. witness mismatch after truncating the agent's local entries) has nothing to run.

Add:

### `POST /verify/compare`
```json
// request
{ "entries": [ /* array of the agent's local entries, same shape as /entries payloads */ ] }
// response
{ "mismatches": [ { "seq": 17, "reason": "missing_locally" | "hash_mismatch" | "extra_locally" } ], "match_count": 41 }
```
Build a small script in `attacks/` (e.g. `compare_local.py`) that reads the agent's local SQLite, sends its entries to this endpoint, and prints the mismatches. This is what T2d, A3, and A7 actually run against — update `05-self-tests.md` and `07-attacks.md` to call `/verify/compare` by name instead of just "`/verify`" for anything that compares local vs. witness state. Plain `/verify` stays for range-checking the witness's own copy against itself (used by the auditor tab, Step 12).

